# Always Build After Changes

After any code change requested by the user (Swift sources, Package.swift, resources, etc.):

1. Build before considering the task done.
2. Prefer: `swift build --build-path /tmp/zinc-build` (repo `.build` often hits `build.db` disk I/O errors under Documents).
3. After code changes, also bundle the app: `BUILD_PATH=/tmp/zinc-build ./scripts/bundle.sh` so `Zinc.app` is runnable with Accessibility.
4. Fallback: `swift build` from the repo root if `/tmp` is unavailable.
5. If the build fails, fix the errors and rebuild until it succeeds.
6. Report the build result briefly (success or the failing error).

Do not skip the build even for small edits. Use full permissions (`all`) so SPM can write its build database. Run the app via `open Zinc.app`, not the raw binary in `.build` or `/tmp`.
